                'excerpt' => 'Learn how modern enterprises navigate hardware refresh cycles, safeguard corporate data, and recoup maximum asset value through structured ITAD.',
                'content_blocks' => json_decode('[{"type": "html", "content": "<h2>Navigating Modern IT Asset Disposition</h2><p>IT Asset Disposition (ITAD) has evolved from a back-office logistics task into a boardroom strategic priority. With enterprise hardware lifecycles averaging three to four years, corporate technology officers face dual imperatives: preventing catastrophic data breaches while fulfilling environmental sustainability commitments.</p><h3>Key Pillars of a World-Class ITAD Program</h3><ul><li><strong>Audited Chain of Custody:</strong> GPS-tracked sealed transport and barcoded bin scanning from office pickup to destruction facility.</li><li><strong>Certified Data Sanitization:</strong> Adherence to NIST Special Publication 800-88 Revision 1 guidelines for magnetic and flash media.</li><li><strong>Component Value Recovery:</strong> Testing and harvesting functional enterprise CPUs, high-density ECC RAM, and enterprise NVMe drives for secondary remarketing.</li></ul><p>By implementing a proactive ITAD framework, organizations routinely recover between 15% and 35% of original hardware acquisition costs while maintaining bulletproof compliance audits.</p>"}]', true),
