                'image_path' => 'blog_images/hard-disk-destruction.jpg',
                'excerpt' => 'Understand when high-coercivity electromagnetic degaussing is required versus industrial dual-shaft mechanical shredding.',
                'content_blocks' => json_decode('[{"type": "html", "content": "<h2>Physical Media Destruction: Mechanics and Security</h2><p>When high-security regulations (such as HIPAA, GDPR, or defense sector contracts) require total physical elimination of storage media, organizations must decide between electromagnetic degaussing and mechanical shredding.</p><h3>High-Coercivity Degaussing</h3><p>Degaussers generate intense magnetic pulses (often exceeding 10,000 to 20,000 Gauss) that permanently disrupt the magnetic domains on spinning hard disk platters and tape cartridges. This renders magnetic tracks permanently unreadable.</p><h3>Industrial Multi-Shaft Shredding</h3><p>Mechanical shredders utilize counter-rotating hardened steel cutting blades that crush, tear, and fracture storage devices into irregular fragments measuring 20mm or smaller. Shredding is universally applicable across traditional HDDs, solid-state drives, optical media, and smart cards.</p>"}]', true),
