                'image_path' => 'blog_images/api-development.jpg',
                'excerpt' => 'Design scalable microservices, implement OAuth2/mTLS authentication, and maintain granular telemetry for mission-critical workflows.',
                'content_blocks' => json_decode('[{"type": "html", "content": "<h2>The Foundation of Modern Distributed Architecture</h2><p>APIs are the digital nervous system of the modern enterprise. As companies connect disparate ERPs, supply chain logistics engines, and customer portals, API security posture directly dictates overall system resilience.</p><h3>Core Pillars of Enterprise API Security</h3><ul><li><strong>Mutual TLS (mTLS):</strong> Enforcing two-way cryptographic verification between microservices to prevent man-in-the-middle exploits.</li><li><strong>Rate Limiting & Token Bucket Algorithms:</strong> Defending endpoints against Denial of Service (DoS) and credential stuffing attacks.</li><li><strong>Granular Scope Authorization:</strong> Implementing role-based access control (RBAC) and attribute-based access control (ABAC) embedded in signed JWT assertions.</li></ul>"}]', true),
